<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter I, Grand Duke of Oldenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1755">1755</a>–<a href="/years/1829">1829</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Peter Frederick Louis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Frederick Louis ruled Oldenburg from 1785, first as regent for his cousin and from 1823 as duke in his own right. A careful administrator, he lost his duchy when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> annexed it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1811 but regained it in 1813. Oldenburg became a grand duchy at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> and gained the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birkenfeld">Birkenfeld</a> in 1817.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-i-grand-duke-of-oldenburg.jpg" alt="Peter I, Grand Duke of Oldenburg" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Friedrich Adolph Schöner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_I_Oldenburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
